
# Cron and Crontab

## Cron
- Used to schedule tasks
- Runs automatically

## Crontab
- Stores scheduled job
- crontab -e → edit

## Format
- MIN HOUR DOM MON DOW CMD

## Fields
- MIN → minute
- HOUR → hour
- DOM → day of month
- MON → month
- DOW → day of week
- CMD → command

## Example
- 0 * /12 * * * cp -R /home/... /var/backups/

## Notes
- * → any value
- Used for automation (e.g., backups)


# Package Management

## Repositories
- Software stored in repositories
- Located in: /etc/apt

## Important Files
- sources.list
- sources.list.d

## Add Repository
- add-apt-repository

## GPG Keys
- Verify software authenticity
- Ensure trusted downloads


# Installing Software

## Update
- apt update

## Install
- apt install <package>

## Remove
- apt remove <package>


# Logs in Linux

## Location
- /var/log

## Purpose
- Monitor system health
- Track activity
- Detect issues or attacks


# Types of Logs

## Apache Logs
- access.log → requests
- error.log → errors

## Other Logs
- auth.log → authentication
- syslog → system activity
- fail2ban.log → brute force attempts
- ufw.log → firewall logs
